<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">River Liffey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The River Liffey rises in the Wicklow Mountains and flows in a wide loop through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kildare">Kildare</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> Bay, dividing the city of Dublin into north and south. The Norse founded their settlement at Dublin near its mouth in the 9th century. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it marked the southern edge of the kingdom of Brega.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/river-liffey.jpg" alt="River Liffey" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dave Meier · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:River-liffey.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
